Subject: CVE-2026-118764 — adapt cli-v3 forcedExternal filters for minimatch 11

minimatch 11 removed the standalone makeRe export and does not compile a regexp. trigger.dev v4.8.x cli-v3 still imports makeRe for forcedExternal glob filters. Match with Minimatch. esbuild 0.23 registers onResolve filters as filter.source and never calls RegExp.test, so literal package names use a real RegExp and every callback rejects non-matches before the collected-external fast path.

Origin: DHI-internal (DHI build harness)
CVE: CVE-2026-118764
Description: Replace makeRe with Minimatch matching. Literal forcedExternal names get a real RegExp source; callbacks reject non-matches before the collected-external fast path.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/triggerdotdev/trigger.dev.git 645cc47dd2eeb99387f604cad2c90ba2ef568680 packages/cli-v3/src/build/externals.ts
Verify: cmd `pnpm --dir packages/cli-v3 exec tsx src/build/forcedExternalResolve.esbuild.test.ts` expect "forced-external esbuild regression ok"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI override pins minimatch 11 for CVE-2026-118764 until upstream adopts minimatch 11)
Drop-When: never: drop when upstream packages/cli-v3 no longer imports makeRe from minimatch (or ships an equivalent minimatch-11-safe forcedExternal path)

